Fri Nov 20 19:26:52 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- New package uutils-coreutils 0.13.0, replacement for
  GNU coreutils; upstream tag 0.13.0 verified, 2026-11-20.
- GNU compatibility: sort option checks, date case flags,
  dd conv fixes, ls time-style, tail symlinks, printf and
  friends aligned with GNU.
- Safer handling: cp via symlinks, mv/ln dir checks,
  chown/chgrp preserve-root, install backup, rm escape.
- Faster and robust: panics fixed, non-UTF-8, basenc 35x,
  cut/date/join faster; WASI tests; 684/707 GNU pass.
- Packaging: Conflicts/Provides coreutils plus single/systemd
  and doc/systemd-doc splits (9.12), no Obsoletes so the switch
  happens only on explicit install; SKIP hostname/more/kill;
  ships [, libstdbuf, man and completions; tests run in
  -test flavor; vendor MIT audited.

